ve grown up in a health-conscious childhood home.\n\n4.**If people have good relationships with their parents, then they fulfill their nutritional daily intakes.**\n   - This means that if someone has a good relationship with their parents, they are likely to fulfill their nutritional daily intakes.\n\n5.**If people have good relationships with their parents, then they do not eat salads regularly.**\n   - This suggests that if someone has a good relationship with their parents, they are unlikely to eat salads regularly.\n\n6.**If people visit the gym at least once a day, then they always fulfill their daily nutritional intakes.**\n   - This implies that if someone visits the gym at least once a day, they are likely to fulfill their daily nutritional intakes.\n\n7.**It is either both true that Taylor grew up in a health-conscious childhood home and she has a good relationship with her parents, or it is true that Taylor neither grew up in a health-conscious childhood home nor has a good relationship with her parents.**\n   - This provides two possible scenarios for Taylor: either she grew up in a health-conscious childhood home and has a good relationship with her parents, or she did not grow up in a health-conscious childhood home and does not have a good relationship with her parents.\nBased on the analysis, it is clear that Taylor is certain to eat salads regularly, regardless of the scenario. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n# Certain. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
