ctive and disinterested members of the community chaperone high school dances.\n   - Young children and teenagers who wish to further their academic careers and educational opportunities are students who attend the school.\n\n2.**Statement Breakdown**:.\n   - The statement claims that if Bonnie is either a young child or teenager who wishes to further her academic career and educational opportunities and chaperones high school dances, or neither is a young child nor teenager who wishes to further her academic career and educational opportunities, then she is either a student who attends the school or an inactive and disinterested member of the community.\n\nThe statement is false because it inaccurately reflects the conditions under which Bonnie can be classified as either a student who attends the school or an inactive and disinterested member of the community.. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
