messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nIf people work in student jobs on campus, then they need to earn money to help pay for their college tuition. If people order takeout frequently in college, then they work in student jobs on campus. People either order takeout frequently in college or enjoy the dining hall meals and recipes. If people enjoy the dining hall meals and recipes, then they are not picky eaters. If people enjoy the dining hall meals and recipes, then they spend a lot of their time eating and catching up with friends in the campus dining halls. If Mary works in student jobs on campus and needs to earn money to help pay for her college tuition, then Mary is neither picky nor needs to earn money to help pay for her college tuition.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or uncertain? Mary either is not a picky eater or, if she is, then she spends a lot of her time eating and catching up with friends in the campus dining halls.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Uncertain', '<think>.\nTo determine the truth value of the statement "Mary either is not a picky eater or, if she is, then she spends a lot of her time eating and catching up with friends in the campus dining halls," we need to analyze the given information step by step.\n\n1.**Identify the given information:**.\n   - If people work in student jobs on campus, then they need to earn money to help pay for their college tuition.\n   - If people order takeout frequently in college, then they work in student jobs on campus.\n   - People either order takeout frequently in college or enjoy the dining hall meals and recipes.\n   - If people enjoy the dining hall meals and recipes, then they are not picky eaters.\n   - If people enjoy the dining hall meals and recipes, then they spend a lot of their time eating and catching up with friends in the campus dining halls.\n   - Mary works in student jobs on campus and needs to earn money to help pay for her college tuition.\n\n2.**Analyze the implications:**.\n   - Since Mary works in student jobs on campus, she needs to earn money to help pay for her college tuition.\n   - This implies that Mary either orders takeout frequently in college or enjoys the dining hall meals and recipes.\n   - If Mary enjoys the dining hall meals and recipes, then she is not picky eaters.If Mary doesn\'t enjoy the dining hall meals and recipes, then she doesn\'t spend a lot of her time eating and catching up with friends in the campus dining halls.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
