messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nAll employees who schedule a meeting with their customers will appear in the company today. Everyone who has lunch in the company schedules meetings with their customers. Employees will either have lunch in the company or have lunch at home. If an employee has lunch at home, then he/she is working remotely from home. All employees who are in other countries work remotely from home. No managers work remotely from home. James is either a manager and appears in the company today or neither a manager nor appears in the company today.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or uncertain? James has lunch in the company.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Uncertain', '<think>.\nTo determine whether the statement "James has lunch in the company" is true, false, or uncertain, let\'s analyze the given information step by step:.\n\n1.**All employees who schedule a meeting with their customers will appear in the company today.**.\n   - This means that if an employee schedules a meeting with their customer, they must be present in the company.\n\n2.**Everyone who has lunch in the company schedules meetings with their customers.**.\n   - This implies that if an employee has lunch in the company, they are also scheduling meetings with their customers.\n\n3.**Employees will either have lunch in the company or have lunch at home.**.\n   - This indicates that employees have two options for lunch: either in the company or at home.\n\n4.**If an employee has lunch at home, then he/she is working remotely from home.**.\n   - This suggests that if an employee chooses to have lunch at home, they are not physically present in the company.\n\n5.**All employees who are in other countries work remotely from home.**.\n   - This means that if an employee is in another country, they are working remotely from home.\n\n6.**No managers work remotely from home.**.\n   - This implies that if an employee is a manager, they cannot be working remotely from home.\n\n7.**James is either a manager and appears in the company today or neither a manager nor appears in the company today.This gives us only one possible scenario for James: he is a manager and appears in the company today, or he is not a manager and does not appear in the company today.\n\nNow, let\'s consider the statement "James has dinner in the company."We need to evaluate this based on the given information:.\n\n- If James is a manager and appears in the company today, then according to point 6, he cannot be working remotely from home.Therefore, he must not be having dinner in the company.\n- If James is not a manager and does not appear in the company today, then he cannot not be having dinner in the company because he is not present in the company.\n\nGiven these conditions, we can conclude that the statement "James has dinner in the company" is certain because it depends on whether James is a manager or not.If he is a manager, he might not have dinner in the company; if he is not a manager, he definitely has dinner in the company.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is:.\nB) Certain.\n</think>.\n<answer>\n. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
