e hanging out with and playing with their siblings, they often did not live at home regularly.\n\n3.**Apply the relationships to Luke**:.\n   - We know that Luke either is both a twin or triplet and develops strong bonds with his family members, or he neither is a twin or triplet nor develops strong bonds with his family members.\nDespite the lack of direct information about Luke\'s complaints regarding annoying siblings in the context, it is stated that complaining about annoying siblings is common among people with siblings of the same age.\n\n4.**Inference**:.\n   - Due to the absence of details about Luke\'s complaints, we can neither confirm nor deny the veracity of the statement with the information given.\n\nHence, the accurate response is:.\nA) True.\n</reflect>.\n<response>\n. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
