ing second to the left of E, let's analyze the given information step by step:\n\n1. **Positioning A and B**: A sits second to the right of B. This means that if we start from B, A is two seats to the right of B.\n\n2. **Positioning C and D**: C and D are immediate neighbors of A and B respectively. This means that C is one seat to the left of A and D is one seat to the left of B.\n\n3. **Positioning E**: E is not an immediate neighbor of either A or B. This means that E is not one seat to the left or right of A or B.\n\n4. **Positioning G and H**: G is third to the right of H. This means that if we start from H, G is three seats to the right of H.\n\n5. **Positioning F**: F is not an immediate neighbor of A. This means that F is not one seat to the left or right of A.\n\nNow, let's arrange the people around the circular table based on the given information:\n\n- B is at the starting point.\n- A is two seats to the right of B, so A is at the 3rd position.\n- C is one seat to the left of A, so C is at the 2nd position.\n- D is one seat to the left of B, so D is at the 4th position.\n- E is not an immediate neighbor of either A or B, so E must be at the 5th position.\n- G is third to the right of H, so G is at the 7th position.\n- H is not an immediate neighbor of D, so H must be at the 6th position.\n- F is not an immediate neighbor of A, so F must be at the 1st position.\n\nNow, we need to determine who is sitting second to the left of E. Since E is at the 5th position, the person sitting second to the left of E is the person at the 3rd position, which is A.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is:\n\nA) A",
